      "nodeType": "claim",
      "title": "Equal areas of the four midpoint triangles",
      "summary": "For a nondegenerate triangle ABC with side midpoints D, E, and F, the four triangles AEF, BFD, CDE, and DEF each have area one quarter of ABC. The theorem remains valid under the corrected altitude relation and is established as an ordinary mathematical proof, not as a machine-checked formalization.",
