      "nodeType": "lemma",
      "title": "Parallelism and half-length relations for triangle midpoint segments",
      "summary": "The midpoint vector identities imply that EF, FD, and DE are respectively parallel to BC, CA, and AB and have half their corresponding lengths. These relations support half-scale similarity of the medial triangle and the corner-triangle area arguments.",
